course: dictionary
lesson: 8619
title: Screwdriver: a tool that turns screws
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A screwdriver is a tool you hold to turn screws in or out. It has a handle you grip and a metal tip that fits into the top of a screw. Look for the tip in the word's context: the tip is the part that does the turning.
explain: «Push down on the long handle of a screwdriver jammed under a paint tin lid, and the short end near the rim pushes up so hard that the lid pops off.» Here the screwdriver is used as a lever, so the long handle is the part you push. Pushing the long handle gives you power at the short end.
explain: «A wheel and axle turns a big wheel with a small force into a strong twist on the small axle; door handles, steering wheels, taps and fat screwdriver handles use it.» Handles that turn are clues: the wide grip of a screwdriver is shaped so your hand can give it a strong twist.
fact: A screwdriver is a tool with a handle and a metal tip.
fact: The tip fits into the top of a screw, and you turn the handle to move the screw.
fact: Two common types are the flat-head screwdriver and the Phillips (cross-head) screwdriver.
fact: Remember «righty-tighty, lefty-loosey»: turn clockwise to tighten a screw, and anticlockwise to loosen it.
fact: People use screwdrivers to build furniture, open battery covers on toys and fix things.
exercise: What is a screwdriver used for? | To measure how much water is in a jug | *To turn screws in or out | To cook an egg | To cut paper into shapes
exercise: Which way do you turn a screw to tighten it? | Anticlockwise, to the left | Straight up into the air | Side to side, like a wave | *Clockwise, to the right
exercise: In «Push down on the long handle of a screwdriver jammed under a paint tin lid», which part do you push down on? | The short end | The rim of the tin | *The long handle | The paint inside the tin
test: What part of a screwdriver fits into the top of a screw? | The paint tin lid | The wooden handle | *The metal tip | The rim
test: Name two common types of screwdriver. | Hammer and saw | *Flat-head and Phillips (cross-head) | Wooden and plastic | Red and blue
exam: Why would you use a screwdriver to open a battery cover on a toy? | To make the toy louder | *To turn the screw that holds the cover on | To paint the cover a new colour | To pour water into the battery
